{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured and verified a persistent CentOS 5 iptables firewall on node1. SSH remains allowed from any IPv4 source; TCP/9000 is accepted only from node2 (10.100.85.11) and explicitly rejected from node3 and all other sources. All three nodes were restarted sequentially and recovered with changed boot identities.","actions_performed":["Preserved the installed CentOS 5.11 release and 2.6.18-398.el5 kernel.","Backed up node1's original firewall configuration.","Added ordered TCP/9000 source-allow and fallback-reject rules while retaining the any-source SSH rule.","Saved the rules to /etc/sysconfig/iptables and enabled iptables for runlevels 2–5.","Verified node2 received HTTP 200 on TCP/9000, node3 was rejected, and both retained SSH access.","Restarted node1, node2, and node3 individually, waiting for full recovery before proceeding.","Repeated firewall behavior checks after restarts and removed the temporary TCP/9000 test listener."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent host firewall and legacy-platform compatibility","command_ids":["cmd-033aaa3162be4889","cmd-b56eeb774e2a466e","cmd-ceb66868331a49be"],"summary":"Shows identical live and persisted rules, iptables boot enablement, CentOS 5.11/kernel 2.6.18 retained, and the firewall remaining active after test-listener cleanup."},{"requirement":"SSH allowed from any address","command_ids":["cmd-256d2d6dff1849b3","cmd-bf8bb9e71cdc44ce","cmd-b56eeb774e2a466e"],"summary":"Node2 and node3 both successfully connected to node1 SSH; final rules and counters show the unrestricted TCP/22 ACCEPT rule."},{"requirement":"TCP/9000 allowed only from node2 and rejected from node3/everywhere else","command_ids":["cmd-256d2d6dff1849b3","cmd-bf8bb9e71cdc44ce","cmd-ce03f1ce917f4a5b","cmd-b56eeb774e2a466e"],"summary":"Node2 received HTTP 200, node3 received a failed connection, and firewall counters recorded both ACCEPT traffic from 10.100.85.11 and fallback REJECT traffic. The persisted fallback rule covers every other IPv4 source."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ce03f1ce917f4a5b","cmd-7f5eb811b75c44fd","cmd-794eb9fe37ef419e","cmd-6335597fc8964c0c","cmd-3c6931acc58d4a2a","cmd-9c3b3e15677f4240"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 55fc4a00-9697-494d-8000-000000000000, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID cf35d2dc-5db7-4808-8000-000000000000, recovered SSH and firewall rules, followed by successful node2 allow and node3 reject tests."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-3c6931acc58d4a2a","cmd-4c7db92f97e346af","cmd-6a52dcf0d8bc4ed6","cmd-2c44745bd4d54f2c"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 9b2c3c8a-2d02-42dc-8000-000000000000, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID 6669d4f7-b705-45d2-8000-000000000000, and recovered SSH plus permitted TCP/9000 connectivity."},{"requirement":"Node3 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-c52eaa244c9045c6","cmd-b137f97b851e4415","cmd-598f1be4e2dc41fd"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID c362e1bd-f5c0-4758-8000-000000000000 and reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID 638caed5-6622-49c8-8000-000000000000, recovered SSH, continued node1 SSH access, and continued TCP/9000 rejection."}]}
